<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy sets 11.0 trillion lire repo tender.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy sets 11.0 trillion lire repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it called a 11.0 trillion lire repurchase tender for today for government securities to be resold on March 21.</p>
<p>At the previous comparable operation for 9.5 trillion lire on February 12, the minimum accepted rate stood at 7.41 percent and the average rate at 7.43 percent.</p>
</text>
